.TH "libnvmf_config_validate" 9 "libnvmf_config_validate" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_config_validate \- dry-run a connection configuration.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_config_validate
.BI "(struct libnvme_global_ctx *ctx "  ","
.BI "const char *file "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "ctx" 12
libnvme global context
.IP "file" 12
main configuration file, or NULL for the default.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads and resolves like \fBlibnvmf_config_read\fP, reporting every
diagnostic through \fIctx\fP, without handing back a configuration.
.SH "RETURN"
0 when the configuration is valid (including absent),
negative errno otherwise.
